<title>GERMANY: TABLE - E.German May industry orders up 3.8 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>TABLE - E.German May industry orders up 3.8 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     May 97   April 97     May 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +3.8	 +4.7	 +9.8</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +11.9	+18.3	-14.6</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		158.7	152.9	141.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				  May 97  April 97    May 97 index</p>
<p> Domestic orders	     +7.5	+4.5	175.4</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Apr/May 97 with Feb/Mar 97:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		  +9.0</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Apr/May 97 with Apr/May 96:</p>
<p> Manufacturing orders		 +16.9</p>
<p> Domestic orders			 +9.5</p>
<p> Foreign orders			 +53.7</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +20.0</p>
<p> Capital goods			  +15.7</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	    +7.9</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
